KZ3 patch 2047 (RSX pass 47): draw payload cache for the live renderer's vertex fetch.
LD_VTX_CACHE=0|1|verify (default LD_VTX_CACHE_DEFAULT): a draw whose vertex payload and topology indices come only
from guest memory no tracked writer touched since they were fetched replays the bytes it uploaded then (ring memcpy)
instead of reading the indices, remapping, fetching and rebuilding the topology. Key = the full fetch state of the
draw (primitive, layout, per used attribute type/size/stride/frequency/offset/location and the current value of the
disabled ones, base offset/index, divider mask, index array, restart, the draw's batches), compared word by word.
Validity per source span (index range, each attribute's element range from the fetch plan): no tracked write this
frame (page bitmap), none since the fill (per-page frame stamps set at the flip), and a sampled content hash (9 x 16
bytes) unchanged, against untracked writers replacing a whole buffer. Local memory only unless LD_VTX_CACHE_MAIN=1;
filled at the second sight of a key; an entry invalidated twice by tracked writes stays uncached; budget
LD_VTX_CACHE_MB (256). verify = fetch every hit as before and compare byte for byte ([vtx-cache-bad]). Statistics:
[vtx-cache] every 256 frames with RSX_PERF=1. Off under the diagnostic dumps that read the CPU-side payload.
Pass 49: LD_VTX_CACHE_FULL=1 (default) validates a hit with a full compare of the source bytes against a copy kept at
the fill (spans merged per location; the copy counts against the budget); 0 = the round-47 sampled hash.
